; error: 18:11: 'c' is given as 'value 1' too, and the call changes it through 'value 1' while it reads it through 'value 2'; a place the call changes is given once, so keep a copy of it in a variable first, and give that as the other
; A call of a task value gives a place it changes once, as a named call does.
task bump(hold& n: int)
    n = n + 1
fi

task both(hold& a: int, bind& b: int)
    a = b
fi

task squares(r: region, n: int) -> [int]@r
    <- new [int]() at r
fi

task main()
    hold c = 1
    bind f = both
    f(&c, &c)
fi
